---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LevelLadder from '../components/LevelLadder.astro';
import Level from '../components/Level.astro';
import Status from '../components/Status.astro';
import { load, url, fmtDate, KIND_LABEL } from '../lib/site';
const { organs, technologies, specimens, developments } = await load();
const counts = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map((n) => specimens.filter((s) => s.data.level === n).length);
const highest = Math.max(...specimens.map((s) => s.data.level));
const latest = developments.slice(0, 5);
---
<Base title="Sovereign Agents" section="home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">A reference on autonomous AI agents</p>
      <h1>What it takes for software to keep itself alive</h1>
      <p class="lede">A sovereign agent holds its own keys, pays for its own compute, and runs where no single party can read or stop it. This reference sets out what such an organism needs, who has attempted it, and which technologies can supply it today.</p>
      <div class="census" role="list">
        <div role="listitem"><b>L{highest}</b><span>Highest level observed in a tracked system</span></div>
        <div role="listitem"><b>{specimens.length}</b><span>Systems assessed against one framework</span></div>
        <div role="listitem"><b>{organs.length}</b><span>Organs an organism needs to survive</span></div>
        <div role="listitem"><b>{technologies.length}</b><span>Technologies assessed for maturity</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="pillars" aria-label="Sections">
      <div class="pillar">
        <p class="kicker">Blueprint</p>
        <h2><a href="/blueprint/">What an organism needs</a></h2>
        <p>Nine organs, from keys to an immune system, each with the threat it faces, the best current options and the part nobody has solved. A six-level framework and a reference build path.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/blueprint/anatomy/">Anatomy</a><span>{organs.length} organs</span></li>
          <li><a href="/blueprint/framework/">Levels and axes</a><span>L0–L5</span></li>
          <li><a href="/blueprint/build-path/">Reference build path</a><span>to L3</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <p class="kicker">Ecosystem</p>
        <h2><a href="/ecosystem/">Who has tried</a></h2>
        <p>Notable attempts at an autonomous agent, scored on five axes with evidence and an assessment date, and a log of the developments that changed what is possible.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/ecosystem/tracker/">Tracker</a><span>{specimens.length} systems</span></li>
          <li><a href="/ecosystem/developments/">Developments</a><span>{developments.length} entries</span></li>
          <li><a href="/ecosystem/builders/">Builders</a><span>who supplies the parts</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <p class="kicker">Technology</p>
        <h2><a href="/technology/">What is available</a></h2>
        <p>Explainers on the components an organism is built from, from confidential computing and threshold keys to payment rails and self-replication, each with a maturity assessment and its failure modes.</p>
        <ul>
          {technologies.slice(0, 3).map((t) => <li><a href={url.tech(t.id)}>{t.data.title}</a></li>)}
          <li><a href="/technology/">All {technologies.length} technologies</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2>The state of the field</h2><a href="/ecosystem/tracker/">Open the tracker →</a></div>
      <p class="finding">No tracked system has reached L3. Several have made their keys unreadable to their host, and one framework keeps them out of any single machine. None yet combines that with income of its own, more than one hardware vendor, and upgrades no single party controls. L3 can be assembled from parts that ship today.</p>
      <LevelLadder counts={counts} />
      <table class="matrix" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <thead><tr><th>Highest assessed</th><th>Level</th><th class="hide-sm">Status</th><th class="hide-sm">Lesson</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {specimens.slice(0, 4).map((s) => (
            <tr><th><a href={url.specimen(s.id)}>{s.data.name}</a></th><td><Level n={s.data.level} /></td><td class="hide-sm"><Status value={s.data.status} /></td><td class="hide-sm muted">{s.data.lesson}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2>Recent developments</h2><a href="/ecosystem/developments/">All developments →</a></div>
      <ol class="devlog devlog-compact">
        {latest.map((d) => (
          <li><time datetime={d.data.date}>{fmtDate(d.data.date)}</time><div><span class="tag" data-k={d.data.kind}>{KIND_LABEL[d.data.kind]}</span><h3>{d.data.title}</h3><p>{d.data.summary}</p></div></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
